-- title:
--   Mod p weight-2m functions on X₀(N) lift, K algebraically closed
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$, let $N \ge 1$ be an integer with $p \nmid N$, let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $m \ge 1$ be a natural number. Work inside the field $K((q))$ of Laurent series, written as `LaurentSeries K`, with $\bar\jmath =$ `jqModC K` the series $q^{-1}$ times the reduction of the numerator power series `jNum`, and $\bar\jmath_N =$ `jqNModC K N` its image under $q \mapsto q^N$. Let $G$ be an element of the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldC K N`, i.e. of $K(\bar\jmath, \bar\jmath_N) \subseteq K((q))$, and assume `IsModPFormFn K m` holds for $G$: that $G^{6}\,\bar\jmath^{\,4m}(\bar\jmath - 1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\bar\jmath$, and $G^{2}\,\bar\jmath^{\,m}(\bar\jmath-1728)^{m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\bar\jmath^{-1}$. Then there is a power series $\varphi \in K[[q]]$ lying in [`ModPForms.modPMod N (2 * m) K`](def/CuspForm_ModPForms.html#L12) — the $K$-span of the series $\sum_n \overline{a_n} q^n$ arising from integer sequences $(a_n)$ that are the $q$-expansion coefficients of a modular form of weight $2m$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ — whose image in $K((q))$ equals `qexpOfWeight K m G`, that is $G \cdot (\theta\bar\jmath)^{m}$, where $\theta\bar\jmath =$ `thetaJ K`.
--
--   This is the algebraically closed case of the passage from holomorphic weight-$2m$ modular functions on $X_0(N)$ in characteristic $p$, presented as $G$ with $G\,(\theta\bar\jmath)^m$ its weight-$2m$ $q$-expansion, to the Serre–Swinnerton-Dyer space of reductions of $q$-expansions of classical integral weight-$2m$ forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$; it is the converse direction to [`ModPForms.exists_isModPFormFn_qexpOfWeight_eq_of_mem_modPMod`](thm.html#ModPForms.exists_isModPFormFn_qexpOfWeight_eq_of_mem_modPMod). It is used to obtain the statement over a general field of characteristic $p$ and in the computation of traces of Hecke-type correspondences on this space.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModPForms_exists_mem_modPMod_ofPowerSeries_eq_qexpOfWeight_of_isModPFormFn_of_isAlgClosed.lean

